    {
      "rule_key": "BIAYA_JABATAN",
      "rule_version": "ID-2026.1",
      "calc_type": "PERCENTAGE_CEILING",
      "provenance": "OFFICIAL",
      "source_note": "PMK 250/2008 Pasal 1 (biaya jabatan / occupational cost: 5% of gross income, capped Rp500.000/bulan = Rp6.000.000/tahun). DOCUMENTATION-ONLY row: this figure is consumed INLINE by PPH21_ARTICLE17's occupational_cost_bp/occupational_cost_cap_annual_minor (the December Art-17 true-up, phase P3) — no pay_component references BIAYA_JABATAN directly.",
      "effective_from": "2026-01-01",
      "params": {
        "ceiling_minor": 6000000,
        "employee_bp": 500,
        "employer_bp": 0,
        "reduces_tax_base": true
      }
    },
    {
      "rule_key": "BPJS_KESEHATAN",
      "rule_version": "ID-2026.2",
      "calc_type": "PERCENTAGE_CEILING",
      "provenance": "OFFICIAL",
      "source_note": "Perpres 64/2020 Pasal 30 (Jaminan Kesehatan Nasional iuran): employer 4%, employee 1%, base capped at Rp12.000.000/bulan. The employee 1% leg is NOT deductible from the PPh21 base; the employer 4% leg IS a taxable fringe benefit to the employee (raises the tax base only, never gross earnings/net cash). P7 REVIEW W5 FIX (ID-2026.2, supersedes the ID-2026.1 row): base_kind=BASE_PAY — the statutory spec (§3.1, the BPJS matrix) bases every BPJS leg on WAGE (pokok + tunjangan tetap), never on a commission/overtime/THR-laden taxable gross; ID-2026.1 shipped with the base_kind field OMITTED (defaulting to TAXABLE_GROSS), an oversight this version corrects. APPROXIMATION (documented, ADR 0031 P7 addendum): 'base pay' here is engine's PersonInput.basePay — the person's aggregated comp-package base ONLY; fixed allowances (tunjangan tetap) are not yet a distinct, separately-summed input this engine models, so a company paying meaningful fixed (non-variable) allowances alongside base pay under-bases BPJS relative to the true statutory wage until that modeling lands — a tracked follow-up, not silently claimed complete.",
      "effective_from": "2026-01-01",
      "params": {
        "ceiling_minor": 12000000,
        "employee_bp": 100,
        "employer_bp": 400,
        "reduces_tax_base": false,
        "employer_adds_to_tax_base": true,
        "base_kind": "BASE_PAY"
      }
    },
    {
      "rule_key": "BPJS_JHT",
      "rule_version": "ID-2026.2",
      "calc_type": "PERCENTAGE_CEILING",
      "provenance": "OFFICIAL",
      "source_note": "PP 46/2015 (Jaminan Hari Tua): employer 3.7%, employee 2%, uncapped base (modeled with the agreed unbounded sentinel 999999999999 minor — never a real ceiling). The employee 2% leg IS deductible from the PPh21 base (December true-up); the employer 3.7% leg is NOT a taxable fringe benefit. P7 REVIEW W5 FIX (ID-2026.2, supersedes ID-2026.1): base_kind=BASE_PAY — see BPJS_KESEHATAN's source_note for the full rationale + the fixed-allowances-not-yet-modeled approximation this shares.",
      "effective_from": "2026-01-01",
      "params": {
        "ceiling_minor": 999999999999,
        "employee_bp": 200,
        "employer_bp": 370,
        "reduces_tax_base": true,
        "employer_adds_to_tax_base": false,
        "base_kind": "BASE_PAY"
      }
    },
    {
      "rule_key": "BPJS_JP",
      "rule_version": "ID-2026.2",
      "calc_type": "PERCENTAGE_CEILING",
      "provenance": "OFFICIAL",
      "source_note": "PP 45/2015 (Jaminan Pensiun): employer 2%, employee 1%, base capped at the annually-announced JP ceiling (Rp10.547.400/bulan as of this dataset's authoring). WARNING: the JP ceiling is ADJUSTED EVERY MARCH by BPJS Ketenagakerjaan announcement — verify the current figure against the latest announcement before/at activation and PATCH this rule with the corrected ceiling_minor if it has changed. The employee 1% leg IS deductible from the PPh21 base; the employer 2% leg is NOT a taxable fringe benefit. P7 REVIEW W5 FIX (ID-2026.2, supersedes ID-2026.1): base_kind=BASE_PAY — see BPJS_KESEHATAN's source_note for the full rationale + the fixed-allowances-not-yet-modeled approximation this shares.",
      "effective_from": "2026-01-01",
      "params": {
        "ceiling_minor": 10547400,
        "employee_bp": 100,
        "employer_bp": 200,
        "reduces_tax_base": true,
        "employer_adds_to_tax_base": false,
        "base_kind": "BASE_PAY"
      }
    },
    {
      "rule_key": "BPJS_JKK",
      "rule_version": "ID-2026.2",
      "calc_type": "PERCENTAGE_CEILING",
      "provenance": "OFFICIAL",
      "source_note": "PP 44/2015 (Jaminan Kecelakaan Kerja): employer-only, rate by COMPANY risk class I-V (I 0.24%, II 0.54%, III 0.89%, IV 1.27%, V 1.74%). This row encodes the DEFAULT class II rate (0.54%) only, uncapped base; a per-company risk-class attribute plus a dedicated risk-class calc family to select among the five rates is a documented follow-up (ADR 0031) — until then every tenant is seeded at class II regardless of its real registered risk class. The employer leg IS a taxable fringe benefit to the employee. P7 REVIEW W5 FIX (ID-2026.2, supersedes ID-2026.1): base_kind=BASE_PAY — see BPJS_KESEHATAN's source_note for the full rationale + the fixed-allowances-not-yet-modeled approximation this shares.",
      "effective_from": "2026-01-01",
      "params": {
        "ceiling_minor": 999999999999,
        "employee_bp": 0,
        "employer_bp": 54,
        "reduces_tax_base": false,
        "employer_adds_to_tax_base": true,
        "base_kind": "BASE_PAY"
      }
    },
